  "strategy": "approach_and_rationale: \n  We address the minimum overlap problem by minimizing the correlation overlap through bipartite graph-based Hopf algebra optimization. This method reparametrizes the step function as a vertex partition on a cycle graph topology, leveraging autocorrelation structure constraints and solvable perturbation analysis around parent solutions. The core contribution is a symplectic integrator with combinatorial gradient descent conditioned on maximum overlap lags.\n\n  mathematical_specification: \n  Represent the step function h as a density matrix in SU(1,1). Define h(x) \u2248 \u03a6(x) where \u03a6(x) is characterized by Kaehler potential K(z) = -ln(1 - |z|^2) and coordinares z \u2208 \u2102/\u2124\u2082. The objective function is:\n  C_5 = \\max_k [(1/h^{(k)})\u2202t(h^{(k)})]_{t=\u221e}\n\n  Constrain h to trace-normalized density matrices with support over [0,2]. The optimization variables are complex amplitudes {a_j} for Chebyshev basis expansion.\n\n  constraints: trace(h) = 1, 0 \u2264 h \u2264 1 (implemented as reflector constraints).\n\n  formulation: Minimize C_5 subject to the linear constraints and use augmented Lagrangian penalty terms for boundary enforcement.\n\n  solver: Custom symplectic integrator with SU(1,1) rotations integrated with graph neural layers.\n\n  implementation_procedure: \n  1. Global initialization: Use parent solution to initialize target rotation axes.\n  2. Local search: Project parent onto Kaehler manifold via BCS/LDA embedding.\n  3. Perturbation schedule: https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Approximate_Bayesian_computation\n  4. Objective tracking: Track spectral radius of transition operators.\n  5. Termination: When expected improvement < 1e-8\n\n  search_choices: \n  - Topology: Two-tiered bubble chamber graph\n  - Discretization: 100 to 500 nodes per coset\n  - Refinement: Adaptive binning based on pion decay length\n\n  budget_and_robustness: \n  Time: 1100s budget allocated proportionally (90% to global search, 10% to local tuning)\n  Hardware: 1 CPU used, multithreaded FFT-based overlap estimator\n  Fallback: Polynomial regression interpolation on coarse grids\n\n  validation: \n  Check numerical s-convergence at fine grid levels.\n  Perform phase space volume invariant test.\\n",
